cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Catalaunian Fields, 451: A Documentary Apparatus"
message: "If you use this apparatus, please cite it as below, and cite the printed source for any passage you quote."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fassbender
    given-names: Pantaleon
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6683-3617"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pantaleonfassbender-coder/The-Catalaunian-Fields"
url: "https://the-catalaunian-fields.netlify.app/"
abstract: >-
  A documentary apparatus for Attila's invasion of Gaul in 451, the battle on
  the Catalaunian fields and its afterlife to 1918, built on the disagreement
  of the sources: five modules with 121 passages, each read against the page
  image of a public-domain printing, the Latin beside the English. Priscus in
  Bury's English (1923); Jordanes' Getica in Mommsen's Latin with a new English
  translation; the chronicles of Prosper, Hydatius, Cassiodorus, Marcellinus,
  Isidore, the Gallic chronicles and the continuations of Prosper (MGH Chronica
  minora); Gregory of Tours (Arndt 1884, Dalton 1927); the Lives of Anianus,
  Lupus and Genovefa with their editor Krusch's verdicts (1896); Sidonius'
  panegyric and letters; and the reception in Gibbon (1788), Creasy (1851),
  Wilhelm II's Bremerhaven speech (1900) and Kipling (1914). With nine
  comparisons, a timeline, fourteen public-domain plates, and a list of what
  is not carried and why. Companion game: Bellum atrox.
keywords:
